{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_D5Pp8FmfXQPe6eVprD2xA2AA","content":"1\t# Literature host interfaces · plan r4\n2\t\n3\t**Status: r4 draft, 2026-11-23. Not reviewed and not approved.** r4 is r2\n4\twith the owner's rulings on D6, D9 and D10, given in the planning session on\n5\t2026-11-22 (r3), and on D17, given on 2026-11-23 (r4). Each is tagged `(o)`\n6\tat its sites; §11 lists what changed. r2 and r3 were never committed. The\n7\tfour rulings settle four decision rows; they do not approve the plan. No plan review has run over any\n8\tof these bytes: no review instrument was selected (decision D14). No plan-gate\n9\trecord exists. The owner gates the plan before any spec is approved and before\n10\tany code.\n11\t\n12\tThis plan covers [#216](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/216)\n13\tand [#215](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/215). It delivers\n14\tthe interface half of the \"host-scale reading and extraction\" carryover from\n15\tthe [literature-depth close](../../literature-depth/016-milestone-close.md).\n16\tThe run over a separately selected corpus and provider budget stays carried\n17\twith the literature-identity follow-up, as that close assigned it.\n18\t\n19\t**Provenance.** Outline r1 is the previous bytes of this file (sha256\n20\t`abefb05f7fa7c19d068182eeeb557efea36bbc89d555647d98ec350b1017bea0`, commit\n21\t`0cf94434`, merged in PR 219). Its phase IDs LH1–LH4 and decisions D1–D3 are\n22\tkept. Its reviews, `.gnd-planning/reviews/pr-219-r2/` and `pr-219-panel/`,\n23\tread the roadmap outline, not these bytes. Every sentence new in r2, r3 or r4 carries\n24\tno review opinion. Every code citation was re-read on 2026-11-22 at `4ad0d216`;\n25\t`src/gnd/examples/literature/` is unchanged since `0f39c392`, where the outline\n26\tcited it. The outline wrote the two module paths without `src/gnd/`; they are\n27\t`src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py` and\n28\t`src/gnd/examples/literature/assertion_admission.py`. Below, `reading.py`,\n29\t`assertion_admission.py` and `depth.py` mean the files in that folder.\n30\t\n31\t## Goal and completion predicates\n32\t\n33\tA host with its own corpus and its own model calls the two literature examples\n34\tas library functions instead of reimplementing them. The examples stay\n35\texamples: neither is promoted to stable CLI (both issues say so).\n36\t\n37\t- **LH1.** `reading.py` has a public producer protocol. `run()` drives the six\n38\t  stages with a caller's producer over a caller's input root: its own\n39\t  documents, its own reading model with its own includes, no saved responses\n40\t  and no producer pin. Each of the fixture-only steps runs on caller data or\n41\t  is recorded as skipped. The run has a byte budget per document as well as\n42\t  the global one, and its caps are parameters. The responses and review\n43\t  receipts a live run produces are retained in its run folder.\n44\t- **LH2.** `replay()` re-derives a live LH1 run from its run folder and the\n45\t  caller's input root with zero producer calls and zero reviewer calls. It\n46\t  takes every setting from the run, and refuses a changed response, receipt or\n47\t  input.\n48\t- **LH3.** `assertion_admission.py` admits assertions of a caller-named entity\n49\t  in a caller's model. An assertion is identified by its own handle `(o)`.\n50\t  Every fact row attached to an admitted assertion is kept, whatever its fact\n51\t  type, together with the facts of the entities reached from it `(o)`. Absent\n52\t  optional facts are simply absent. An include root is admitted.\n53\t- **LH4.** Which values make a supported assertion admissible is caller data.\n54\t  A supported assertion that fails those rules has a status of its own. The\n55\t  target cap is a parameter.\n56\t\n57\tThe milestone is closed when each phase has its record and the close record\n58\tcites green focused lanes for LH1–LH4, the structure and inventory guards,\n59\t`uv run ruff check src tests tools`, the replies drafted for #216 and #215, and\n60\tthe close review. Baseline, measured 2026-11-22 at `4ad0d216` with gnd 0.4.0:\n61\t`uv run pytest -q tests/test_ld3_reading_workflow.py tests/test_ld4_revision.py\n62\ttests/test_ld5_verdict.py tests/test_li4_assertions.py tests/test_li5_lineage.py\n63\t--tb=short` gave `90 passed in 166.21s`; `uv run ruff check src tests tools`\n64\texits 0; the whole-repository `uv run ruff check` exits 1, as it did at the\n65\tinclude-root-routes close, in scripts this milestone does not touch.\n66\t\n67\t## 0. Binding design rules\n68\t\n69\t- **R0.1 Formats stay.** The stage record (`stage-N.json`), the attempt rows\n70\t  and their three outcomes, and the coverage rows with their eight states are\n71\t  unchanged; #216 says they work as they are. `literature-rebind/1` belongs to\n72\t  `interop.py` and is not touched.\n73\t- **R0.2 Packaged bytes stay.** With no new argument, the three packaged\n74\t  reading scenarios and the packaged admission write the bytes they write\n75\t  today. The comparison goes through `tests/support/recorded_version.py`,\n76\t  because the reading run retains two fidelity reports that carry\n77\t  `gnd_version` (H11).\n78\t- **R0.3 Example status stays.** Public here means named in the example's\n79\t  README and covered by tests. No `gnd` subcommand is added, and the two\n80\t  module command lines keep every argument they have.\n81\t- **R0.4 One loop, one walk.** The caller route and the packaged route run the\n82\t  same stage loop and the same projection. The packaged shape becomes default\n83\t  data for that code, not a second copy of it (standing rule 4).\n84\t- **R0.5 A setting is retained evidence.** Every argument that shapes a caller\n85\t  run is written into the run. Replay reads settings from the run, never from\n86\t  its caller.\n87\t- **R0.6 Skipped is not passed.** A step the caller did not supply is recorded\n88\t  with the status `skipped`. No report presents it as qualified, as measured\n89\t  or as zero.\n90\t- **R0.7 The stable commands stay the judges.** `gnd extract`, `verify`,\n91\t  `check`, `fidelity` and `judgments check` are invoked as today. Neither\n92\t  example re-implements one of their checks or widens one of their caps.\n93\t- **R0.8 A parameter has a ceiling.** Each cap that becomes a parameter has a\n94\t  hard maximum fixed in its spec, and a time-bound test at that maximum\n95\t  (standing rule 2).\n96\t\n97\tThe project's six standing rules\n98\t(`.codex/skills/process-phase/references/project.md`) bind every phase; each\n99\tspec discharges them by name.\n100\t\n101\t## 1. Scope, sources and authority\n102\t\n103\tHarvested obligations. \"Observed\" means re-read or run on 2026-11-22 at\n104\t`4ad0d216`; \"inherited\" means claimed by a source and not re-measured;\n105\t\"proposed\" means new in this plan.\n106\t\n107\t| # | Source | Obligation | Kind | Phase |\n108\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n109\t| H1 | #216 \"Problem\" | `run()` (`reading.py:562`) builds `SavedProducer(inputs.responses)` at `:566`; only the private `_evaluate(..., producer=)` at `:445` takes another | observed | LH1 |\n110\t| H2 | `reading.py`, `ReadingInputs` | the root is bound to saved responses by the pin (`:72-75`, \"saved producer table differs from its pin\") and by the roster check (`:113`, \"saved response roster differs\"), and to the packaged vocabulary (`:135`) | observed | LH1 |\n111\t| H3 | `reading.py`, stage loop | seven fixture bindings, the outline's six and the producer label: the `unavailable` scenario names `study-methods` (`:448`); `_calibrate` names that section, the fact `approximation` (`:317`) and `CALIBRATION_FACTS` (`:42`, `:311-327`), and the absence floor is the literal `[2, 2]` (`:372`); `_combined` adds `LABEL` to every population (`:48`, `:247`); `_public_results` needs `conflict.json`, `conflict.txt`, a `subject_label` fact with exactly two labels and exits 1 from `verify` and `check` (`:395-407`); `absence_status` needs the predicate `alternative_integrator` (`:373`); `_review_attempts` needs a `reviews.json` receipt bound to each accepted response's facts digest (`:198-209`); the extraction sidecar names its producer `saved-public-fixture` (`:264`) | observed | LH1 |\n112\t| H4 | `reading.py`, producer boundary | `produce(stage, section)` gets two names and no source bytes (`:156`); the loop reads a `calls` attribute from the producer (`:457`). `_inspect` accepts exactly three outcomes, `accepted`, `empty`, `refused` (`:185`). The outline's \"and the existing others\" was wrong: the other five coverage states are decided by the loop before or without a call | observed | LH1 |\n113\t| H5 | `depth.py:21-30`, `:56`, `:61` | three fixture-scale limits the outline did not list: every input file, source documents included, is read with a 128 KiB cap (`INPUT_LIMIT`); every JSON input is capped at 1 MiB; every `gnd` route has 30 seconds and 1 MiB of output (`PROCESS_LIMITS`). A caller document over 128 KiB refuses at read | observed | LH1 (D4) |\n114\t| H6 | `reading.py:27-30`, `:86`, `:263`, `:298`, `:384-387` | file names are fixed: the eleven `INPUTS` are all required; a source's path must be `<id>.txt`; the model must be `reading.orm.json` with one include named `vocabulary.orm.json`; the artifact names `reading.orm.projection.schema.json` and `reading.orm.applicable.json` are literals. Probe: `gnd extract caller.orm.json` on a renamed copy exits 0 and names its artifacts `caller.orm.*` | observed | LH1 |\n115\t| H7 | `reading.py:386`; include-root-routes IR2 | the loop runs `gnd extract` on the reading model after the producer has answered. `gnd extract` refuses a temporal model. A caller's reading model must be one `gnd extract` accepts, and a refusal there should cost no producer call | observed | LH1 |\n116\t| H8 | `reading.py:473-478`, `:172-174` | the global \"stop\" is a reason computed after the loop; the only thing that ends reading early is the byte budget, which omits sections. \"Per